d.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268614}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f9a5c122-9fbb-5128-a8f8-39c71927c4cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-75004" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\sqrt{t},\\,t-3⟩,$ $|r(5)|=$" :question/worked-solution "Evaluating the function at $t=5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(5) & =⟨\\sqrt{5},\\,5-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{5},\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(5)| & =\\sqrt{{(\\sqrt{5})}^{2}+{(2)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5+4} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
